      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y=-(x-5)(x+7).$",
      "worked_solution": "From the equation $y=-(x-5)(x+7),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=-7.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+(-7)}{2} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-1.$",
