      "dom_id": "question-223666",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(x-1)(x-9)$ is $x=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "From the equation $y=(x-1)(x-9),$ we can tell that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=9.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=5.$",
